## Usage
- `clusters` lists the Clusters of the Instance (at least one). Topics and ACLs of an environment mapped to the Instance are created on every one of them.
- Removing a Cluster from `clusters` also removes its schema registry configuration. Platform Manager refuses it while a Kafka Connect or Flink cluster is registered on that Instance-Cluster.
- `granular_browse_permission` turns on per-topic browse permissions; manage them with `axual_topic_browse_permissions`.
- `authentication_methods` must be methods the tenant supports. Platform Manager enables `MUTUAL_TLS` when it is not set, and refuses removing a method that is in use.
- Leaving out `ca_certificates`, `authentication_methods` or `properties` keeps what the Instance has. `properties = {}` removes all properties. `ca_certificates = []` removes all CA certificates. Platform Manager refuses that with "SSL enabled, but CA was not uploaded." while `MUTUAL_TLS` is enabled and a Cluster of the Instance has `ssl_auth_mode = "fullChainCertificate"`.
- An Instance can only be deleted when no environment, Kafka Connect cluster, Flink cluster or connector deployment uses it.
- The `axual_instance` data source looks up an existing Instance.

## Prerequisites
- With `MUTUAL_TLS` enabled and a Cluster with `ssl_auth_mode = "fullChainCertificate"`, `ca_certificates` must hold the CA that signs application certificates.

## Platform Manager version
- Platform Manager 15.0.9 or later. `flink_enabled = true`, and `connect_enabled = true` without `connect_urls`, need Platform Manager 16.0.0 or later; with an older one, the plan fails.
- Newer Platform Manager versions switch Connect and Flink on for the whole tenant, with the tenant settings `connectRuntimeEnabled` and `flinkRuntimeEnabled`, which this provider does not manage. There `connect_enabled` and `flink_enabled` change nothing: the value is kept only in the Terraform state, and `true` gives a warning on every plan.
- Platform Manager refuses a change of `short_name` while the Instance has environments. Platform Manager does not move the schema registry secrets of the Instance-Clusters when `short_name` changes: 15.0.x and 16.0.x lose the whole schema registry, newer versions its password and private key. The next plan shows it, and the next `terraform apply` configures it again from `axual_instance_cluster`.
- On Platform Manager 15.0.x, adding or removing a Cluster resets `oauth_enabled` of the schema registry of the other Clusters of the Instance. The next `terraform apply` sets it again from `axual_instance_cluster`.

## Required Roles
- TENANT_ADMIN

